# Git Large File Storage (Git LFS)

## Purpose

Git LFS is designed to manage large binary files that are
not efficient to store directly in regular Git history.

## Media File Types

Git LFS can be used for suitable large files such as:

- .psd
- .wav
- .mp4
- .fbx
- .blend

## Benefits

- Keeps the main Git repository lighter.
- Tracks versions of large media assets.
- Supports collaboration on media projects.

## Implementation Plan

Git LFS will be configured locally to track selected large
binary file types. Large files will be tested before submission.

## Important Note

This document describes the planned configuration.
Actual Git LFS tracking must be configured and tested separately.
